                                                "sense_id": "a6ad5a12-758c-3e06-be90-ce3191109796",
                                                "text": "to spell the helmsman"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b7745cc0-2c9d-36e6-97d6-469d35f01a04",
                                        "entry_id": "5f7714b2-5096-3ef7-8ebc-313e6b128ad0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To rest (someone or something), to give someone or something a rest or break."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cd6d2947-9d6c-4cb0-a714-6ea5bc38396f",
                                                "sense_id": "b7745cc0-2c9d-36e6-97d6-469d35f01a04",
                                                "text": "They spelled the horses and rested in the shade of some trees near a brook."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ddcc2197-e27b-31e3-be83-81ec79007d1e",
                                        "entry_id": "5f7714b2-5096-3ef7-8ebc-313e6b128ad0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To rest from work for a time."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "colloquial",
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "spell",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6d0dcb93-5adf-3e8b-93c7-61222f86e039",
                                        "entry_id": "ea37e688-bfa4-3001-979c-f5cec6fcc28d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A shift (of work); (rare) a set of workers responsible for a specific turn of labour."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b30cf0ad-3c58-3c3e-9438-664b5278953e",
                                        "entry_id": "ea37e688-bfa4-3001-979c-f5cec6fcc28d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A definite period (of work or other activity)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "informal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "27f9fe4b-a49a-49e0-a32b-b3e68e3c1d3b",
                                                "sense_id": "b30cf0ad-3c58-3c3e-9438-664b5278953e",
                                                "text": "A chap named Eleazir Kendrick and I had chummed in together the summer afore and built a fish-weir and shanty at Setuckit Point, down Orham way. For a spell we done pretty well. Then there came a reg'lar terror of a sou'wester same as you don't get one summer in a thousand, and blowed the shanty flat and ripped about half of the weir poles out of the sand."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7eeb4f7b-bce9-4891-a9ee-cb150b6fa18e",
                                                "sense_id": "b30cf0ad-3c58-3c3e-9438-664b5278953e",
                                                "text": "I had a job in the great North Woods / Workin' as a cook for a spell / But I never did like it all that much / And one day the ax just fell"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eafd9dda-c3b3-4fba-9087-f9477caf0b65",
                                                "sense_id": "b30cf0ad-3c58-3c3e-9438-664b5278953e",
                                                "text": "Despite his ill-fated spell at Anfield, he received a warm reception from the same Liverpool fans he struggled to win over before being sacked midway through last season."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5da10047-4cab-3fc4-9f56-727fd228802c",
                                        "entry_id": "ea37e688-bfa4-3001-979c-f5cec6fcc28d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An indefinite period of time (usually with a qualifier); by extension, a relatively short distance."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "colloquial"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ec468013-2cd7-4fff-952b-6b824db98afb",
                                                "sense_id": "5da10047-4cab-3fc4-9f56-727fd228802c",
                                                "text": "Even Mrs. Harker seems to lose sight of her trouble for whole spells. [...] When he had spoken, Mina's long spell of silence made me look at her."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9eddd4d3-8aab-44e5-8db7-89c58d4d9403",
                                                "sense_id": "5da10047-4cab-3fc4-9f56-727fd228802c",
                                                "text": "So after a short spell in the brass foundry the wisest course was to follow with a similar period in the steel foundry, where much important work was done, including the manufacture of centres for wheels."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b3490926-a9b9-4bb1-8bdb-113c2453f44e",
                                                "sense_id": "5da10047-4cab-3fc4-9f56-727fd228802c",
                                                "text": "[...] Class 37s became synonymous with the depot, and over the years more than a third of the class had a spell allocated to the shed."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f8797759-0dfa-3630-b535-d44563890982",
                                        "entry_id": "ea37e688-bfa4-3001-979c-f5cec6fcc28d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A period of rest; time off."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "026b3caf-1282-3970-b54b-4cfc7c07d177",
                                        "entry_id": "ea37e688-bfa4-3001-979c-f5cec6fcc28d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A period of illness, or sudden interval of bad spirits, disease etc."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "US",
                                            "colloquial"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e7b66b84-e6ca-3289-a543-0711a4873718",
                                        "entry_id": "ea37e688-bfa4-3001-979c-f5cec6fcc28d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An uninterrupted series of alternate overs bowled by a single bowler."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "spell",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4ba71d34-ba36-324f-ba75-3191bf5e6022",
                                        "entry_id": "b9b3dc6b-ccc1-3f04-bffd-967280b03b94",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A splinter, usually of wood; a spelk."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Northern-England"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2b837c11-1f18-4cae-ad47-c17a983b4924",
                                                "sense_id": "4ba71d34-ba36-324f-ba75-3191bf5e6022",
                                                "text": "To swadle a bowe much about wyth bandes, verye seldome dothe anye good, excepte it be to kepe downe a spel in the backe."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b381c49c-b211-3b2a-8a4e-a32c14651896",
